OpenSSL 4.1.0: an ECH rejection after a HelloRetryRequest ends with illegal_parameter

Upstream code: the ssl/statem/statem_clnt.c hunk of OpenSSL PR #33233 (open, in review), verbatim. Its test hunks
(test/ech_test.c, test/ech_corrupt_test.c) are omitted: the bundled build is configured with no-tests.
PR #33233 head commit: TODO(owner): fill in the PR head commit hash this hunk was taken from.
Carried by Kuicksilver under ADR-0019 (docs/adr/0019-openssl-4-and-ech.md), the second of the two carried patches (applied
after openssl-4.1.0-ech-hrr-custom-ext.patch); pinned by its SHA-256 in gradle/openssl.toml as patch_2, applied by
tools/openssl/apply-patch.pl to the verified tarball, and dropped with the first OpenSSL release that has the PR's fix.

The bug: tls_process_server_hello aborts with illegal_parameter when the ServerHello does not confirm ECH and the
HelloRetryRequest before it carried an encrypted_client_hello extension, taking the extension's presence for an
acceptance, where RFC 9849 section 6.1.4 has the client compare its payload. A server that rejects ECH may send that
extension with eight random octets (RFC 9849 section 7.1), so a client whose ECH a server rejects after a
HelloRetryRequest never reaches the rejection path of RFC 9849 section 6.1.6 (authenticate the public_name, ech_required,
retry_configs). Also, the fallback to the public_name ran at the HelloRetryRequest and again at the ServerHello, leaking
the real server name and reporting the public_name as the inner one.

The fix: after a HelloRetryRequest, the client keeps the HelloRetryRequest's verdict (success) and aborts with
illegal_parameter whenever the ServerHello's confirmation disagrees with it, in either direction (RFC 9849 section 6.1.4:
acceptance "is determined by the server's initial message"); the public_name fallback runs only once, at the first
ServerHello or HelloRetryRequest.

diff --git a/ssl/statem/statem_clnt.c b/ssl/statem/statem_clnt.c
index c79d914c76a78..1b1347ae95b36 100644
--- a/ssl/statem/statem_clnt.c
+++ b/ssl/statem/statem_clnt.c
@@ -1951,6 +1951,14 @@ MSG_PROCESS_RETURN tls_process_server_hello(SSL_CONNECTION *s, PACKET *pkt)
         && s->ext.ech.done != 1 && s->ext.ech.ch_depth == 0
         && s->ext.ech.grease == OSSL_ECH_NOT_GREASE
         && s->ext.ech.attempted_type == TLSEXT_TYPE_ech) {
+        /*
+         * At the ServerHello after a HRR, success still says whether that
+         * HRR accepted ECH. If it didn't, we already fell back to the
+         * public_name when processing the HRR.
+         */
+        int after_hrr = !hrr && s->hello_retry_request != SSL_HRR_NONE;
+        int hrr_accepted = after_hrr && s->ext.ech.success == 1;
+
         if (!set_client_ciphersuite(s, cipherchars)) {
             /* SSLfatal() already called */
             goto err;
@@ -1993,6 +2001,14 @@ MSG_PROCESS_RETURN tls_process_server_hello(SSL_CONNECTION *s, PACKET *pkt)
             OSSL_TRACE_END(TLS);
             s->ext.ech.success = 1;
         }
+        if (after_hrr && s->ext.ech.success != hrr_accepted) {
+            /*
+             * the HRR and SH.random ECH acceptance signals disagree,
+             * so that's an illegal protocol error
+             */
+            SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_ILLEGAL_PARAMETER, SSL_R_ECH_REQUIRED);
+            goto err;
+        }
         if (!hrr && s->ext.ech.success == 1) {
             if (ossl_ech_swaperoo(s) != 1
                 || ossl_ech_intbuf_fetch(s, &abuf, &alen) != 1
@@ -2007,16 +2023,7 @@ MSG_PROCESS_RETURN tls_process_server_hello(SSL_CONNECTION *s, PACKET *pkt)
              * the outer CH, so we better set the hostname for the
              * connection accordingly.
              */
-        } else if (!hrr && s->ext.ech.success == 0
-            && s->ext.ech.hrrsignal_p != NULL) {
-            /*
-             * we previously saw a good HRR ECH acceptance but now
-             * the SH.random ECH acceptance signal is bad so that's an
-             * illegal protocol error
-             */
-            SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_ILLEGAL_PARAMETER, SSL_R_ECH_REQUIRED);
-            goto err;
-        } else {
+        } else if (!after_hrr) {
             OSSL_TRACE1(TLS, "ECH falling back to public_name: %s\n",
                 s->ext.ech.outer_hostname != NULL ? s->ext.ech.outer_hostname : "NONE");
             s->ext.ech.former_inner = s->ext.hostname;
